                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7a48d170-35d1-36d1-a868-28b828b39717",
                        "entry_id": "c1371b7f-597f-3cbd-b6dc-1700b078df3c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Characterised by light; luminous; emitting or manifesting light; radiant."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "literary"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0a68736c-b322-4c8e-b07d-0ee126e202b9",
                                "sense_id": "7a48d170-35d1-36d1-a868-28b828b39717",
                                "text": "While in their mothers wombe enclosd they were, / Ere they into the lightsom world were brought, / In fleshly lust were mingled both yfere […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bbeda533-0e79-4e65-9fbe-bbedd6ed4a3e",
                                "sense_id": "7a48d170-35d1-36d1-a868-28b828b39717",
                                "text": "This said, the smoky cloud was cleft and torn, / Which like a veil upon them stretched lay, // And up to open heav'n forthwith was borne, / And left the prince in view of lightsome day."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a3b15408-3d10-4352-9c0f-7745019b3919",
                                "sense_id": "7a48d170-35d1-36d1-a868-28b828b39717",
                                "text": "There came a day when he remembered the moment, when he regretted that he had not ridden off into the buoyant midst of these lightsome elements."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5d213aea-a85a-4e85-9dba-a4cafe40005f",
                                "sense_id": "7a48d170-35d1-36d1-a868-28b828b39717",
                                "text": "If any find it incredible that Ida be even outwardly so lightsome that she saw clearly in the night, let them answer this question."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cf816202-4981-4835-a672-fa890378827e",
                                "sense_id": "7a48d170-35d1-36d1-a868-28b828b39717",
                                "text": "The literal sense of the Greek is: “If therefore thy whole body is lightsome, having no part darksome, thy whole body will be lightsome, as when the lamp lightens thee with its flashing.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
